2026-06-15 08:55 PT: ADR-070 filed v0.1 (Architect) — MCP-Consumer Connector Architecture. Resolves the architectural-how following PM's 2026-06-14 direction-ratification. Key decisions: (1) Piper as MCP consumer; one Connector protocol (`connect`/`status`/`resolve`/`degrade`) all MCP-consumer adapters implement; (2) ADR-052 reconciled — applies to Piper-as-host (tool surface), ADR-070 to Piper-as-consumer (downstream integrations); no actual tension; (3) MCP server owns OAuth/token lifecycle; Piper stores per-user MCP-server bindings only (not raw creds); (4) DB-backed user-scoped config kills `data/*_preferences.json` cwd-relative flat files; (5) maturity-tiered migration with Slack/Notion escape valve if MCP servers immature; (6) WS-9 identity unification is prerequisite to WS-1, not parallel; (7) frames much of RECONNECT as finishing ADR-058 implementation, not greenfield. Unblocks Lead Dev decomposition. M4/M5 placement is PPM's call.
